# AceUI Project Conventions

## Project Overview

AceUI is a React UI component library using npm workspaces monorepo structure.

## Project Structure

```
aceui/
├── packages/components/{name}/    # Component packages (@aceuidev/{name})
│   ├── src/
│   │   ├── {Name}.tsx
│   │   ├── {Name}.css
│   │   └── index.ts
│   ├── docs/
│   │   ├── .features              # Feature requirements list
│   │   └── todo.md                # Task list based on .features
│   ├── package.json
│   └── tsconfig.json
├── demo/                          # Demo application (Vite)
│   └── src/pages/{name}/          # Component demo pages
└── package.json                   # Root workspace config
```

## Package Naming

- NPM scope: `@aceuidev/{component}`
- Examples: `@aceuidev/button`

## Build Tools

- **Components:** tsup (ESM + CJS + TypeScript declarations)
- **Demo:** Vite

## Naming Conventions

- **Components:** PascalCase (`UserProfile.tsx`, `Button.tsx`)
- **Functions:** camelCase (`getUserData`, `handleClick`)
- **Constants:** UPPER_SNAKE_CASE (`API_BASE_URL`, `MAX_RETRIES`)
- **Files:** kebab-case for non-components (`user-service.ts`, `utils.ts`)

## TypeScript

- Use TypeScript for all files
- Define proper interfaces/types for all props
- Export prop types for documentation
- Use explicit return types for functions
- Avoid `any` type - use `unknown` if necessary

## React & Styling

- Follow `react-components.mdc` for component patterns and performance
- Follow `styling.mdc` for CSS and BEM conventions
- Follow `accessibility.mdc` for A11y standards

## Component Checklist

Before marking a component as complete, verify:
- [ ] TypeScript interfaces defined and exported
- [ ] BEM naming convention followed (`styling.mdc`)
- [ ] CSS file created with proper organization
- [ ] Accessibility attributes added (`accessibility.mdc`)
- [ ] Props properly typed and documented
- [ ] Responsive design implemented (if applicable)
- [ ] Error states handled (if applicable)
- [ ] Loading states implemented (if applicable)
- [ ] index.ts export added

## Creating New Components

Follow the checklist in `README.md` (§ Creating a New Component).
